From 51ab39b4c508a2c6b5b0408920d24e873943e0d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:15:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Policy Routing: the target is an interface; a Status column;
 the Killswitch counts only for an enabled client

Reviewer (long VPN Director experience), three points, all taken as stated:

1. The prohibit must follow the lookup only with the Killswitch on - as
   VPN Director's `from X lookup wgc2` / `from X prohibit` pair does. That
   was already the emitter's shape (pref 9000+code lookup, 9100+code
   prohibit, both families, above main and above VPN Director's band).
   The one delta was that VPN Director also requires the client to be
   ENABLED before it installs its prohibit; ppbr_target() now applies the
   same test (ovpn_is_client_enabled() / wgcN_enable). A switched-off
   client's rules fall through to main - the WAN - instead of blocking.
   The enable toggle fires the same vpnrouting restart the Killswitch
   already used, so reaper_pbr_regen() picks it up with no new hook.

2. The WAN row read "Out the WAN (VPN bypass)" while every VPN row read
   its interface. It reads WAN now; so does the add-rule list, with the
   explanation as a hint when WAN is chosen (the WireGuard pattern).

3. No stories in the Target column: the per-row LAN badge is gone. What a
   target is DOING is a state, so it has its own Status column:
   Active / Active - Killswitch / Inactive - WAN / -. The facts true of
   every rule to an interface (the WireGuard acceleration bypass, what a
   WAN target means) are one note each under the table, as a list.

httpd: the cfg reply's ov[] now means "enabled" (ovpn_is_client_enabled),
as wg[] always did; it used to mean "has an address", which decides
nothing.

Dictionaries, all 25 packs, lockstep 6916 -> 6921: RVR_70 (WAN note),
RVR_71-74 (Status, Active, Inactive, Killswitch) added; RVR_58 (IPv6
hint said a v6-less tunnel always blocks - it is the Killswitch's call
since v3.1.3), RVR_64 and RVR_66 reworded; RVR_23, RVR_65, RVR_68,
RVR_69 retired on their lines.

Static checks 13/13; RT-BE96U MCP built, reaper_verify 28/28 (i18n-quote
clean on the staged page).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
